# ==============================================================================
# NOTES
# ==============================================================================
#
# 1. AWS Region Selection:
#    - Use regions close to your users for lower latency
#    - Consider compliance requirements (GDPR, data residency)
#    - Check service availability (not all services in all regions)
#
# 2. Cost Estimation:
#    - Production config: ~$410/month
#    - Staging config: ~$200/month
#    - Development config: ~$100/month
#    - Use AWS Cost Calculator for accurate estimates
#
# 3. High Availability:
#    - Production: Multi-AZ for all services
#    - Staging: Optional Multi-AZ
#    - Development: Single-AZ to save costs
#
# 4. Backup Retention:
#    - Production: 7 days (or more for compliance)
#    - Staging: 3 days
#    - Development: 1 day minimum
#
# 5. Instance Sizing:
#    - Start conservative, scale based on monitoring
#    - Use CloudWatch metrics to optimize instance types
#    - Consider Reserved Instances for predictable savings
#
# 6. Security Best Practices:
#    - Never commit terraform.tfvars to version control
#    - Store sensitive values in AWS Secrets Manager
#    - Use IAM roles with least-privilege access
#    - Enable encryption at rest and in transit
#
# 7. Network Design:
#    - Public subnets: Load Balancers only
#    - Private subnets: Application workloads (EKS nodes)
#    - Database subnets: Managed services (RDS, Redis, MQ)
#    - Use NAT Gateways for outbound internet access
#
# 8. Database Considerations:
#    - RDS: PostgreSQL with TimescaleDB extension for time-series data
#    - ElastiCache: Redis for caching and session storage
#    - Amazon MQ: RabbitMQ for message queuing
#
# 9. Container Registry:
#    - ECR repositories created for each microservice
#    - Image scanning enabled for vulnerability detection
#    - Lifecycle policies to manage storage costs
#
# 10. Monitoring and Logging:
#     - CloudWatch Logs enabled for all services
#     - CloudWatch Alarms configured for critical metrics
#     - VPC Flow Logs for network troubleshooting
#     - EKS control plane logging enabled
